# These scripts run under Linux - WSL, a build server, or a device host.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout rewrites them with CRLF line
# endings, and a shell script with CRLF fails on its own shebang:
#
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which reads as "bash is missing" rather than "this file was checked out
# wrong". Pin them to LF so the checkout is correct whatever the developer's
# git config says.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.patch     text eol=lf
*.xml       text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
